  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Five dice are rolled and the product of the numbers is recorded. Find the probability that the result is an even number.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{31}{32}$.\n\nUse the complement: the product is odd only when all five dice show odd numbers.",
      "worked": "The product is odd only when all five numbers are odd. Each die has three odd outcomes out of six, and the rolls are independent.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{odd product})&=\\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right)^5\\\\\\Pr(\\text{odd product})&=\\frac{1}{32}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{even product})&=1-\\Pr(\\text{odd product})\\\\\\Pr(\\text{even product})&=1-\\frac{1}{32}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{even product})&=\\frac{31}{32}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
